-- AN ALIAS IS READ FROM THE TENANT'S OWN POSTINGS FIRST.
--
-- Seed rows for layoff_employer_aliases (SPEC 2026-09-18, sections 5 and 10,
-- lane C). The alias table is the only door by which a single-token,
-- ambiguous or CIK-keyed filer reaches a board, so every row here names what
-- was read before it was written, and a rejected row is a refusal the matcher
-- honours and the candidate script never re-proposes.
--
-- BATCH 1, ACCEPTED (238 rows over 173 CIKs, all keyed on cik; relation filer,
-- except the 32 tenant paths that name a subsidiary brand of the filer --
-- Avanade under Accenture, Alexion under AstraZeneca, Versace / Michael Kors
-- / Jimmy Choo under Capri, Solar Turbines under Caterpillar, SimonsVoss
-- under Allegion, iSmash under Assurant, CoverMyMeds under McKesson,
-- Brightree / MatrixCare under ResMed, Slack / MuleSoft under Salesforce,
-- Elsevier / LexisNexis Legal / Reed Exhibitions / Reed Tech under RELX,
-- CenterWell under Humana, Anord Mardix under Flex, ISM under Kyndryl,
-- Boeing's external_subsidiary site, Morningstar DBRS, and FedEx's seven
-- regional FedEx Express / FedEx Trade Networks sites -- which carry
-- relation subsidiary_site so the card prints the spec's parent sentence
-- rather than naming the parent as the board's own employer). The 178
-- slug -> CIK rows of company_financials (migration 20260722234500: exact
-- normalised name against the SEC ticker file, ambiguous brands dropped,
-- served today on the employer lander through get_company_financials), each
-- slug expanded to every catalogue token whose first '~' segment is that
-- slug -- the same join get_company_financials makes at read time. 177 slugs
-- resolve (comcast left the catalogue) to 247 tokens; 4 of those
-- share a slug with a filer they are not (a shooting range, an astrology
-- app, a mutual insurer's tenant) and are REJECTED below with what was read;
-- 5 more are withheld for the owner's read (alias-batch-2). The evidence
-- string names the source migration, the slug and the SEC name.
--
-- REJECTED (52 rows). The seven pairs the never-surface guard plants,
-- the near-misses lanes 1 and 3 called NOT the same, the SEC single-token
-- collisions lane 3 (b) confirmed at exact equality, and the display-name or
-- tenant-path reads made while expanding batch 1. A WARN rejection is keyed
-- on the normalised filer string; an SEC rejection on the filer's CIK; a row
-- carries both keys when both filings exist for the same employer.
--
-- BATCH 2 is NOT in this file. The single-token giants (Oracle, Intel,
-- Conduent, Amentum, RTX, Visa, Chevron, Salesforce, Jabil, Nordstrom,
-- Sharp HealthCare, Owens Corning, Takeda, ...) become accepted rows only
-- after the owner reads three live posting titles from the tenant;
-- scripts/layoff-alias-candidates.mjs prints the queue and turns the ticks
-- into the next migration's rows. This file inserts nothing it did not read.
--
-- Idempotent: one decision per (alias_norm, cik, company_token); a re-run
-- inserts nothing and never overturns a decision the owner changed by hand.
-- alias_norm values were produced by layoff_norm (20260918100100) over the
-- filer strings the lanes recorded; the harness recomputes each one.

SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '2min';

ON CONFLICT (COALESCE(alias_norm, ''), COALESCE(cik, 0::bigint), company_token) DO NOTHING;

-- Self-check on shape, never on counts: a later hand edit (the owner
-- flipping one decision) must not make a re-run of this file fail. Every
-- accepted seed row is cik-keyed with the company_financials evidence, and no
-- (cik, token) pair is both accepted and rejected.
DO $$
DECLARE v_bad int;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO v_bad FROM public.layoff_employer_aliases a
   WHERE a.decided_by = 'seed-20260918200000' AND a.decision = 'accepted'
     AND (a.cik IS NULL OR a.alias_norm IS NOT NULL OR a.evidence NOT LIKE 'company\_financials 20260722234500%');
  IF v_bad > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '% accepted seed rows are not cik-keyed company_financials rows', v_bad;
  END IF;
  SELECT count(*) INTO v_bad FROM public.layoff_employer_aliases a
    JOIN public.layoff_employer_aliases r ON r.cik = a.cik AND r.company_token = a.company_token
   WHERE a.decision = 'accepted' AND r.decision = 'rejected';
  IF v_bad > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION '% (cik, token) pairs are both accepted and rejected', v_bad;
  END IF;
END $$;
